(in-ns 'go.arbace.hs) ^{:go/comments [[15 1 "// Frame is a frame of a thread's stack (HES8 (a))."] [19 15 "// a case's slots; an apply frame's arguments"] [22 11 "// the thread's arena's top when the frame was pushed (arena.go)"] [30 8 "// restores the masking state n on return"] [35 8 "// keepAlive#'s value kept reachable while its action runs"] [38 1 "// Thread is a Haskell thread: its stack, its resumption, its masking state (0 unmasked, 1 masked"] [39 1 "// uninterruptibly, 2 masked interruptibly: getMaskingState#'s numbers)."] [50 23 "// what it waits on: *MVar, *Thunk, *sleep, stmWait, nil when runnable"] [51 23 "// the throwTo#s waiting for it to accept them (rts.go)"] [52 23 "// the TVars its transaction read (a retry's wake-up, the collector's reachability)"] [59 2 "// locked to its capability (forkOn#), and that capability's number (forkOn#'s, modulo enabled_capabilities)"] [62 2 "// bound to an OS thread (the threaded way: the main thread, forkOS's, an in-call's; threaded.go)"] [64 2 "// an interruptible block (MVar, delay, STM retry): an asynchronous exception may be delivered"] [66 2 "// the allocation counter (bytes, counting down), whether its limit is enabled, allocWords when last accounted"] [72 1 "// Machine is hsi's machine: the loader, the address space, the threads."] [82 2 "// the threads waiting on descriptors (fdwait.go) and the last poll of them"] [90 2 "// the weak pointers not yet dead, and the collector's memos of what code keeps alive (rts.go)"] [109 49 "// compiled functions called directly since the last bounce (aot.go)"] [110 49 "// a pure primop's arguments"] [111 49 "// a generic call's arguments (App.eval, applyTmp)"] [112 49 "// a thread's frames at most (SetStackLimit): StackOverflow past it"] [113 49 "// a tail call's arguments"] [117 55 "// a program's own C (cprog.go), or nil"] [118 55 "// objects' identities as C sees them (cprog.go)"] [119 2 "// the RTS's C API (rtsapi.go): the HaskellObj words, stable_ptr_table and its size, the capability's address"] [123 21 "// C finalizers running (runCFins): a callback from one is GHC\\'s error"] [124 21 "// +RTS -xq: the allocation limit's grace, bytes (0: GHC's 100k)"] [125 2 "// the threaded way (threaded.go, HES84 (a)): the program linked -threaded; enabled_capabilities, +RTS -N's count and"] [126 2 "// the label's address; the safe foreign calls in flight and their returns; the spark pool"] [135 2 "// the program's own C threads (queue 430): the ids of the threads its C started (cprog.go's clone), the timespec of"] [136 2 "// cIdle's nap, and each C thread's capability its in-calls are locked to (rts_setInCallCapability)"] [147 1 "// hsFatal is an error of hsi itself (a class at the check: unimplemented, an impossible state)."] [150 1 "// exitNow ends the program (shutdownHaskellAndExit, an uncaught exception in the main thread)."] [157 1 "// NewMachine is a machine over the STG of the units in libs and the program in prog."] [198 2 "// in place (HES73): the popped slot's fields written, no frame copied (its x and n are zero: pop clears them)"] [204 1 "// blockedE is returned by a node whose thread blocked: its resumption is set already."] [207 1 "// enterValue evaluates a value: a thunk entered, anything else returned."] [216 1 "// enter evaluates a thunk: its value, or its code under an update frame, the thunk blackholed."] [234 3 "// another thread evaluates it: wait for its update; a transaction aborts first and reruns from its start"] [235 3 "// after the wake-up (review 189, F2, the user's decision: the other threads never see its writes)"] [253 4 "// two update frames in a row (the lower thunk's evaluation is entering this one): squeezed as GHC's"] [254 4 "// stack squeezing does, the lower thunk an indirection to this one, one frame for both (cgrun060 at"] [255 4 "// +RTS -K64k)"] [256 4 "// (the lower thunks kept blackholed in the frame's env, updated, raised or reverted with it)"] [262 5 "// in place, as pushCase"] [272 4 "// evaluated in place (newThunkN)"] [281 1 "// update overwrites a thunk with its value."] [285 31 "// the fields and the frame may live in the thunk's own allocation"] [299 1 "// apply calls f with args (eval/apply: exact, partial, over-saturated)."] [339 1 "// applyTmp is apply of arguments in a scratch buffer (App.eval's): copied wherever they outlive the call, a partial"] [340 1 "// application one object with its arguments, a partial application saturated straight into the callee's frame."] [396 1 "// ApplyV applies a value to values (a thread's start, a primop's callback)."] [406 1 "// ret handles the top frame on a return."] [409 2 "// the two frequent frames read in place (HES73): no frame copied out, its pointers cleared"] [443 4 "// a queued throwTo# delivered at the unmasking, its value lost as GHC's"] [456 1 "// raiseLam is the code of a thunk whose evaluation raised: entered, it raises again."] [459 1 "// RaiseFree raises its frame's first slot."] [466 1 "// raise raises a synchronous exception (raise#, raiseIO#): the stack unwound to the nearest catch"] [467 1 "// frame, the thunks under evaluation on the way updated to raise it again."] [472 1 "// raiseAsync raises an asynchronous exception in the current thread: the thunks under evaluation on"] [473 1 "// the way reverted to unevaluated (GHC freezes them; the same results)."] [478 1 "// Frozen is an evaluation an asynchronous exception interrupted (HES56 (b), GHC's raiseAsync and AP_STACK): the frames"] [479 1 "// above an update frame, their slots copied, and the control the thread was at, an expression and its slots or a return"] [480 1 "// of r and rs. The update frame's thunk takes it as its code (frozenLam): the next demand pushes the frames back and"] [481 1 "// resumes the control, so the work done is kept (an unsafePerformIO inside runs once, as GHC's)."] [490 1 "// frozenLam is a frozen thunk's code: entered, under its own update frame, it resumes the evaluation."] [511 1 "// frozenIndLam is the code of a thunk squeezed below a frozen one in its update frame: entered, it evaluates that one."] [514 1 "// EnterFree evaluates its frame's first slot."] [521 1 "// copyFramesEnv is copyFrames of fs and a copy of env, the control's slots, sharing the copy with a frame whose slots"] [522 1 "// they are."] [548 1 "// raiseAsyncFrozen raises an asynchronous exception in the current thread, a thread not running whose control is e and"] [549 1 "// env (or a return of r and rs when e is nil), as GHC's raiseAsync: each update frame above the nearest catch frame takes"] [550 1 "// the frames above it and the control as its thunk's frozen code, the next segment's control the demand of that thunk."] [551 1 "// A segment that holds a transaction's frame is not frozen: from it on, unwind's reverting."] [581 1 "// freezeThunk gives a thunk under evaluation the code l over v (raiseAsyncFrozen), unevaluated again; its waiters woken."] [616 5 "// an asynchronous exception is not catchSTM#'s: its nested writes undone, on (review 189, F9)"] [631 1 "// uncaught ends a thread whose exception reached the bottom of its stack (forkIO's and runMainIO's own"] [632 1 "// handlers catch everything, so only a thread started without them gets here: one killed before it ran,"] [633 1 "// which ends silently, as GHC's)."] [641 2 "// a thread killed before it started (forkIO's handler not yet on its stack) ends silently, as GHC's"] [644 1 "// ---- threads ----"] [654 1 "// wake makes a blocked thread runnable."] [664 1 "// block stops the current thread until it is woken; on waking it returns from the blocked call"] [665 1 "// (with the return registers its waker sets) or runs e."] [672 3 "// a queued throwTo# delivered as the thread blocks interruptibly (threadPaused's"] [673 3 "// maybePerformBlockedException; review 189, F5)"] [681 1 "// unblock takes a blocked thread out of what it waits on."] [721 3 "// its throwTo# revoked"] [726 2 "// an interrupted MVar operation leaves no state (review 189, F4)"] [732 1 "// Run runs the program's :Main.main and returns its exit status."] [761 3 "// the program's own C faulted (cprog.go): the process a signal's end, as a C program's"] [784 1 "// reason writes why hsi stopped (HES43 (b)), a word beside its message, on a line of its own: \"hsi-reason: WORD\" (bin/hsi"] [785 1 "// check records it as the result's :reason, a class matches it by its :reasons)."] [788 1 "// fatalReason is the reason of a stop of hsi's own by its message: what it lacks (a primop, a Cmm primcall, a C function,"] [789 1 "// a function pointer, the RTS's API) or a state it cannot go on from (a deadlock), else fatal."] [808 1 "// where describes the current thread's stack for an error message."] [835 1 "// schedule runs threads until until is done (or every thread is)."] [849 6 "// a safe foreign call returning or the first delay expiring, whichever comes first"] [857 6 "// asleep in poll(2) until a descriptor is ready or the first delay expires (awaitEvent)"] [873 5 "// every thread waits for a safe foreign call (the threaded way): until one returns"] [880 4 "// the program's own C threads may still put into an MVar (hs_try_putmvar) or call in: they run first, and"] [881 4 "// while one lives no thread is deadlocked (GHC's: an MVar a C thread can reach by a stable pointer is alive)"] [908 1 "// cIdleNap is the longest nap of cIdle when none of the program's C threads can run now."] [911 1 "// cIdle lets the program's own C threads run while no Haskell thread can (queue 430; the C threads and the machine share"] [912 1 "// crt's baton, one runs at a time): the runnable ones first (crt's Yield), then, when no Haskell thread was woken, a nap of"] [913 1 "// at most d (cIdleNap) in crt's nanosleep, in which the C threads waiting for a time run as it comes. False when the C"] [914 1 "// started no thread or every one it started has ended."] [963 1 "// deadlock is GHC's scheduleDetectDeadlock when no thread can run and none waits for time: a collection (rts.go's"] [964 1 "// gc) resurrects the blocked threads no root reaches; when it resurrects none, the main thread, blocked, gets"] [965 1 "// NonTermination (the non-threaded RTS's last resort). False: nothing to do (hsi stops)."] [977 1 "// runSlice runs t for a time slice, or until it blocks or ends."] [992 5 "// GHC's threadStackOverflow: StackOverflow raised in the thread, asynchronously"] [997 5 "// the allocation limit, checked every 256 bounces (GHC: at each nursery block, 4 KiB)"] [1002 39 "// a transaction is not preempted (HES9 (a))"] [1016 3 "// a case continuation run by ret may be compiled code that ran a yield# or a direct call to the budget's end"] [1017 3 "// (HES74 (c): -O1's inline yield#, a forked thread's first chance): the slice ends here too, as it would"] [1018 3 "// after the interpreter's eval of the alternative"] [1029 1 "// shutdown flushes the standard handles (hs_exit's flushStdHandles) and is the exit status."] [1034 3 "// exitScheduler (threaded.go): the other threads deleted, those in foreign calls left"] [1046 1 "// Exit is the program's end requested by shutdownHaskellAndExit: the handles flushed first."] [1060 1 "// CFunctions are the C functions hsi's table has."] [1069 1 "// PrimopNames are the primops hsi implements."] [1078 1 "// Loaded is the number of modules loaded, LoadedBytes their forms' size, Steps the nodes run (by slices)."] [1083 1 "// defaultStackFrames is a thread's frames at most without -K: 2 GiB of frames (GHC's default is 80 % of the host's"] [1084 1 "// memory, which hsi's frames, larger than GHC's words, would reach later than GHC; a bound keeps an endless recursion"] [1085 1 "// from taking the host: the review of HE4d's runs). Loop's 3,000,000-deep chain needs about 10 million."] [1088 1 "// frameBytes is a frame's size, the unit -K's bytes are counted in (GHC counts its stack's words; a frame of hsi's"] [1089 1 "// holds what a few of GHC's words do, so a -K limit is reached at a comparable depth, not the same one)."] [1092 1 "// SetStackLimit sets a thread's stack limit to bytes (+RTS -K)."] [1101 1 "// unwindThunk is a thunk under evaluation an exception unwinds: reverted to unevaluated (asynchronous), or made to raise"] [1102 1 "// again (synchronous); its waiters woken."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[209 24] [221 27] [252 18] [261 19] [291 23] [411 26] [444 36] [556 7] [556 15] [586 24] [620 37] [674 35] [740 20] [817 27] [817 44] [970 17] [998 44] [1112 24]]} (go/file "machine.go" :imports [


